# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Title #
#, no-wrap
msgid "Hamiltonian simulation {#hamiltonian-simulation}"
msgstr "Simulasi Hamiltonian {#hamiltonian-simulation}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Hamiltonian simulation is a quantum computing technique used to model and characterize quantum systems based on their energy and interactions. It has potential applications in drug discovery and chemistry, battery development, catalyst design, advanced materials, solar energy, and the study of complex physical phenomena such as superconductivity. \n"
msgstr "Simulasi Hamiltonian ialah teknik pengkomputeran kuantum yang digunakan untuk memodelkan dan mencirikan sistem kuantum berdasarkan tenaga dan interaksinya. Ia berpotensi digunakan dalam penemuan ubat dan kimia, pembangunan bateri, reka bentuk mangkin, bahan termaju, tenaga suria, dan kajian fenomena fizikal yang kompleks seperti kebolehkonduksian super. \n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "By simulating molecular interactions and the behavior of electrons and atoms, Hamiltonian simulation can help researchers predict material properties, understand chemical reactions, and identify promising candidates for new technologies. Common approaches include Trotterization, which approximates continuous time evolution using sequences of quantum gates, and sample based quantum diagonalization, which estimates the energy spectrum for a given quantum system.\n"
msgstr "Dengan mensimulasikan interaksi molekul serta tingkah laku elektron dan atom, simulasi Hamiltonian dapat membantu penyelidik meramalkan sifat bahan, memahami tindak balas kimia, dan mengenal pasti calon yang menjanjikan untuk teknologi baharu. Pendekatan biasa termasuk Trotterisasi, yang menghampiri evolusi masa berterusan menggunakan jujukan Gate kuantum, dan pepenjuruan kuantum berasaskan sampel, yang menganggarkan spektrum tenaga bagi sesuatu sistem kuantum.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "A typical workflow starts by mapping a physical system, such as a set of interacting fermions or bosons, onto qubits and circuits. From there, you can reduce the resulting circuit's depth and gate count with compilation and error-mitigation techniques, run the circuit on quantum hardware, and reconstruct the system's properties, such as its ground-state energy, from the measured samples. The tools on this page cover each of these stages, and the application functions listed here provides a single managed workflow for Hamiltonian simulation.\n"
msgstr "Aliran kerja biasa bermula dengan memetakan sistem fizikal, seperti satu set fermion atau boson yang berinteraksi, kepada qubit dan litar. Dari situ, anda boleh mengurangkan kedalaman dan bilangan Gate litar yang terhasil dengan teknik penyusunan dan mitigasi ralat, menjalankan litar pada perkakasan kuantum, dan membina semula sifat sistem, seperti tenaga keadaan asasnya, daripada sampel yang diukur. Alat pada halaman ini merangkumi setiap peringkat ini, dan application functions yang disenaraikan di sini menyediakan satu aliran kerja terurus untuk simulasi Hamiltonian.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Mapping tools {#mapping-tools}"
msgstr "Alat pemetaan {#mapping-tools}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"These capabilities specialize in mapping domain problems into quantum operators and circuits for execution on a quantum computer. Use them to represent fermionic, bosonic, or spin systems, and to compile the resulting circuits so that they run with less depth and fewer entangling gates on quantum hardware.\n"
"<CardGroup>\n"
msgstr ""
"Keupayaan ini mengkhusus dalam memetakan masalah domain kepada operator dan litar kuantum untuk dilaksanakan pada komputer kuantum. Gunakannya untuk mewakili sistem fermion, boson, atau spin, dan untuk menyusun litar yang terhasil supaya ia berjalan dengan kedalaman yang lebih rendah dan Gate berbelit yang lebih sedikit pada perkakasan kuantum.\n"
"<CardGroup>\n"

